  "question": {
    "text": "The variance of the numbers $8,21,34,47, \\ldots, 320$ is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "8788",
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\begin{aligned}\n& 8+(n-1) 13=320 \\\\\n& 13 n=325 \\\\\n& n=25 \\\\\n& \\text { no. of terms }=25\n\\end{aligned}$\n$\\begin{aligned}\n& \\text { mean }=\\frac{\\sum \\mathrm{x}_{\\mathrm{i}}}{\\mathrm{n}}=\\frac{8+21+\\ldots+320}{25}=\\frac{\\frac{25}{2}(8+320)}{25} \\\\\n& \\text { variance } \\sigma^2=\\frac{\\sum \\mathrm{x}_{\\mathrm{i}}^2}{\\mathrm{n}}-(\\text { mean })^2 \\\\\n& =\\frac{8^2+21^2+\\ldots .+320^2}{13}-(164)^2 \\\\\n& =8788\n\\end{aligned}$",
    "image": null
  },
